    {
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1070,
      "width": 738,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1069809876,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1635492426,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783920649071,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "b9H",
      "id": "trace",
      "text": "Traversal: DFS(s), siblings ordered by before-tree.\ns-children {1,3,4}:  before(3)=1 => 3 < 1;  before(4)=1 => 4 < 1.\n3 vs 4: TIE — both are (after=s, before=1) — in BOTH trees. Timestamp must decide.\nOLDER-first  => 3, 4, 1  =>  Text: 341  (correct)\nnewer-first  => 4, 3, 1  (wrong: 3 was displayed left of 4)",
      "originalText": "Traversal: DFS(s), siblings ordered by before-tree.\ns-children {1,3,4}:  before(3)=1 => 3 < 1;  before(4)=1 => 4 < 1.\n3 vs 4: TIE — both are (after=s, before=1) — in BOTH trees. Timestamp must decide.\nOLDER-first  => 3, 4, 1  =>  Text: 341  (correct)\nnewer-first  => 4, 3, 1  (wrong: 3 was displayed left of 4)",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "containerId": null
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1220,
      "width": 882,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 30344153,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1061027670,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1783920649071,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "index": "b9I",
      "id": "warn",
      "text": "Does it hold in general?  Sequential fooling pair for the symmetric splice:\nW1: ins a.1(s,e); ins b.2(s,a); ins c.3(a,e) -> [b,a,c]; del a -> b:(s,e) c:(s,e); must read [b,c]\nW2: ins a.1(s,e); ins b.2(a,e); ins c.3(s,a) -> [c,a,b]; del a -> b:(s,e) c:(s,e); must read [c,b]\nPost-splice states BIT-IDENTICAL, required orders opposite -> no read/tie-break\npreserves delete-order under splice. The lost bit is WHICH SIDE of the dead node\neach survivor was on (b: before=a vs after=a) — i.e. the ghost reference.",
      "originalText": "Does it hold in general?  Sequential fooling pair for the symmetric splice:\nW1: ins a.1(s,e); ins b.2(s,a); ins c.3(a,e) -> [b,a,c]; del a -> b:(s,e) c:(s,e); must read [b,c]\nW2: ins a.1(s,e); ins b.2(a,e); ins c.3(s,a) -> [c,a,b]; del a -> b:(s,e) c:(s,e); must read [c,b]\nPost-splice states BIT-IDENTICAL, required orders opposite -> no read/tie-break\npreserves delete-order under splice. The lost bit is WHICH SIDE of the dead node\neach survivor was on (b: before=a vs after=a) — i.e. the ghost reference.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "containerId": null
    },
